module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_witness_module_outside_the_required_lanes_never_gets_resolved

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_witness_module_outside_the_required_lanes_never_gets_resolved: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_witness_module_outside_the_required_lanes_never_gets_resolved" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "resolution of a claim module is performed by SOMETHING THAT RUNS. Name the module on an admitted required lane (required_gate_prefixes or required_gate_authored_modules), or add a required-lane claim that resolves it as its subject, so an unresolved callee in a witness import block is reported by the gate instead of sitting in the tree. WHEN THIS FIRES: an import fault in this family is found by the required lane at the moment it is introduced, and this row's next-rung trigger is discharged by the gate's own refusal rather than by a session discovering it through a funded acquisition." as NonEmptyStr,
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a claim module that no required lane names can be unresolvable, and nothing reports it. The gate roster decides what is executed (after the 2026-09-19 nominal-roster ruling the required floor executes only modules matching required_gate_prefixes or required_gate_authored_modules), so a module outside both is never resolved by any run — a resolve-time fault inside it is invisible to CI, to the required lane, and to every rung derived from it.",
    "SPECIMEN, MEASURED 2026-11-25 at head 47b6ef2374edea105c1f52cb3269618d90637f00: #test.claim.guarantee_probe_corpus_witness::dark_suite_dispositions_cover_migrated_v1_probes calls distinct_string_count directly, and the file's import block from gunbc.guarantee_measurement imported only that module's wrapper fns, never the callee itself. Every acquisition of the module therefore died at resolve with the hard diagnostic 'effect summary incomplete: call to distinct_string_count ... has no established callee identity' at the call site — including the acquisitions claimed by earlier work on this node, which cannot have executed the leg they reported.",
    "WHY IT SAT UNNOTICED, READ NOT INFERRED: the only files in the repository that name test.claim.guarantee_probe_corpus_witness are artifacts/rung-drops/required_lanes_do_not_resolve_product_layer_modules_2026-09-20.txt lines 1908 and 1910. The artifact that records the decline is the only thing that mentions the module, so the module's unresolvability had no consumer that could notice it.",
    "FIX ON RECORD: commit a7f633d757c added the callee to the import block. After it the module resolves and the leg executes for the first time; its first real verdict was a FAIL carrying the counted uncovered population, and the naming face #test.claim.guarantee_probe_corpus_witness::dark_suite_partition_names_the_uncovered_rows now prints want/got counts and the offending ids instead of an unexplained FAIL.",
    "GENERIC FORM, which is why this is a failure MODE and not an anecdote: the defect class is 'a fault that only execution can report, in a module no required lane executes'. Its detection cost is one funded heavy-slot acquisition per discovery, paid by whoever happens to run the module; its silent cost is any claim about that module's verdicts made without executing it. The fix is not to repair declarations — the live_tree_disposition notes in #gunbc.guarantee_probe_corpus are correct and must not be retyped — it is to give the module a consumer that runs.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
